<title>UK: UK's OFT seeks comments on Norweb,Comet deal.</title>
<headline>UK's OFT seeks comments on Norweb,Comet deal.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's Office of Fair Trading said on Wednesday it asked for comments on the sale by United Utilities unit NORWEB's retail business to Kingfisher's Comet for 51 million stg.</p>
<p>The OFT said it was considering whether the deal qualifies for investigation under the merger provisions of the Fair Trading Act.</p>
<p>If it does the OFT will consider whether to advise the government to refer the merger to the Monopolies and Mergers Commission. -- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717.</p>
</text>
